Let $x=\operatorname{arccot} \frac{4}{7}$. Then $\cot x=\frac{4}{7}$.
Since $\cot x=\frac{1}{\tan x}$, we have $\tan x=\frac{7}{4}$.
Therefore, $\tan \left (\operatorname{arccot} \frac{4}{7} \right)=\boxed{\frac{7}{4}}$.The answer is: \frac{7}{4}

