Using properties of matrix multiplication, we have
\[\mathbf{M}(-2 \mathbf{v} + \mathbf{w}) = \mathbf{M}(-2 \mathbf{v}) + \mathbf{M}(\mathbf{w}) = -2(\mathbf{M} \mathbf{v}) + \mathbf{M} \mathbf{w} = -2 \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 10 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 12 \end{pmatrix}}.\]
The answer is: \begin{pmatrix}5\12\end{pmatrix}

